<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104147" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τμη-τός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cut, shaped by cutting,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἱμάντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					747
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				1245
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τμητοῖς ὁλκοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					863
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυρὸς τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					133.9
				</span></i>
			 (anap.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				30.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>that can be cut</i> or <i>severed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς τὸ τμητικὸν πρὸς τὸ τμητόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					1020b29
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mete.</u>
				387a7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.275
			</span></i>.</div>
